assessment.verification_assessment:
Acceptance is observable. It requires evidence of all of the following:
- the identified Python profile/transport revision and custody;
- instrumented no-Node process and dependency paths;
- real ingress;
- effect dispatch;
- durable consumer outcome and readback;
- restart followed by readback on the production path.

Explicit negative conditions hold the work: a local fake, the Wave 1 receipt or a running tunnel alone is insufficient, and invalid scope or missing readback holds. One independent verdict is meaningful. A fresh verifier retrieves the exact candidate SHA in its own worktree and judges retained evidence against one predicate. That evidence covers revisions, commands, exit statuses, immutable observation references and negative-control counts. Caveat: the verifier judges live-proof observations rather than re-running live effects, so the quality of immutable observation references and the no-Node instrumentation determine how strong the verdict can be.
